apq|n|A company of travelers, pilgrims, or merchants, organized and equipped for a long journey, or marching or traveling together, esp. through deserts and countries infested by robbers or hostile tribes, as in Asia or Africa. ; A large, covered wagon, or a train of such wagons, for conveying wild beasts, etc., for exhibition; an itinerant show, as of wild beasts. ; A covered vehicle for carrying passengers or for moving furniture, etc.; -- sometimes shorted into van.	a:vlo,125,32~vlo,125,32	N:2p5,147,5~2p5,147,5
